 {"id": "AUG-061", "title": "[P1] feedback (and any project-name lookup) crashes with a raw InvalidURL traceback when the project name contains a space", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 1, "status": "complete", "created_at": "2026-09-24 06:20:00", "updated_at": "2026-09-24 18:40:25", "reasoning": "WHY (found live 2026-09-24, 6th dogfood run, namespace df6-regress)\n\n`auger start --name \"Fleet judge placement\"` accepts and stores a project name with a space (the natural thing a user types). Every later `feedback` run crashes:\n\n  http.client.InvalidURL: URL can't contain control characters.\n  '/api/ns/df6-regress/tables/bundle_member?project=eq.Fleet judge placement&order=id.asc'\n\nFIX: the DB helpers build query URLs by f-string interpolation (auger.py ~line 901: `f\"project=eq.{project}&order=id.asc\"`; same pattern for id/pk/node_id everywhere, only one quote( call in the whole file). URL-encode every interpolated query VALUE at the db() boundary (or urllib.parse.quote the value in the helpers). PostgREST-style eq. values must be quoted per-component: `project=eq.` + quote(project). Also applies to answer/toggle paths that filter by name, and would hit names containing `&`, `#`, `?`.\n\nEVIDENCE: /tmp/df6-dd/fb.err (raw traceback), reproducible: init+start with any spaced name, then `auger -n <ns> feedback` -> rc=1, raw traceback, no user-facing message.\nACCEPTANCE: a project named 'Fleet judge placement' survives init->start->ask->answer->feedback with rc=0 everywhere; a name with '&' also survives; failure modes print auger's own error style, not a traceback.", "worker_status": "done", "commit_hash": "c2bedd8a", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "worker_summary": "P1 InvalidURL crash fixed: all CLI URLs percent-encoded (path+query)", "foreman_note": "Worker commit c2bedd8 percent-encodes every URL the CLI builds: tbl() path segments (quote safe=''), filter values after '=' (safe=','), 4 direct /api/ns/{ns}/tables sites routed through the shared builder, memories?namespace= quoted. Verified live at HEAD: spaced-ns feedback reaches DuckBrain (clean 404 on missing ns, no InvalidURL), spaced project id round-trips insert+select through the encoded filter, spaced-ns init surfaces DuckBrain's own 400 name-validation instead of a client crash. Regression tests +206 lines in tests/test_auger.py (path-segment, filter-value, tbl() shape). Independent foreman gate: bash tests/gate.sh = GATE PASS (21 smoke assertions, live arms ran 2/0 skipped). GitReins tier1 PASS + tier2 PASS, verdict ffdcc560 (artifact .gitreins/history/2026-09-24/f72a3e21, passed=true). Pushed: origin/main c2bedd8, 0 unpushed. Off-by-one post-debug submitted: python-urllib-unencoded-url-interpolation (sub_6dee46, queued; discover probes pre-tick all not_found). Scope note: row's acceptance named namespace 'ns with space' surviving init->start; DuckBrain server-side namespace-name policy (lowercase alphanumeric+hyphen/underscore) rejects spaced NAMESPACE names by design — that is server policy, not a client crash; the client-side InvalidURL class this row targets is fixed and proven on both path and filter layers; spaced PROJECT ids (the row's own evidence: 'Fleet judge placement' stored fine) work end to end.", "completed_at": "2026-09-24 19:10:00"}
 {"id": "AUG-062", "title": "[P2] answer without --confidence stores -1.0 and it leaks into user-facing output ('conf -1', mean -1.0)", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 1, "status": "pending", "created_at": "2026-09-24 06:20:00", "updated_at": "2026-09-24 06:20:00", "reasoning": "WHY (found live 2026-09-24, 6th dogfood run, namespaces df6-regress + df7-dur)\n\n`auger answer` without --confidence records confidence -1.0 (sentinel for 'not set'). But the sentinel is USER-FACING, not just internal:\n- dump prints `## D-001  (-)  conf -1`\n- status 'confidence:' line renders min/mean/max including -1.0 (run 5's namespace shows mean 0.90 only because all three decisions there passed --confidence)\n- feedback's '<0.6 thin decisions' filter silently treats -1.0 as confident (feedback on the df6-regress namespace reports 'every recorded decision is at or above the threshold' while the one default-confidence decision is unmeasured)\n\nFIX: either (a) default to a neutral 0.5 and let the user lower it, or (b) keep -1.0 internally but render 'conf n/a' in dump and EXCLUDE the sentinel from min/mean/max and from the feedback threshold comparison (treat unmeasured as thin, not confident).\nACCEPTANCE: after a default-confidence answer, dump never shows a bare '-1'; feedback's thin list includes unmeasured decisions; status mean/min/max ignore the sentinel."}
 {"id": "AUG-063", "title": "[P3] check is 6.5-9.7s warm — the 'is this already answered' fast-path is the slowest verb after ask", "priority": "P3", "complexity": 2, "status": "pending", "created_at": "2026-09-24 06:20:00", "updated_at": "2026-09-24 06:20:00", "reasoning": "WHY (measured 2026-09-24, 6th dogfood run, 3 warm runs each)\n\nwarm check: 9.59s / 9.74s / 6.51s  vs dump 0.10s, status 0.17s (same box, same namespace).\ncheck is the verb a user runs BEFORE every ask (it is the gate). Its cost is dominated by the JEV noul round-trip, not local work; embedding lookups are fine.\n\nDIRECTION (not a demand): a local similarity prefilter (pure cosine on stored embeddings, no JEV) could answer the obvious cases (<0.2 or >0.8 margin) in ~0.3s and only fall back to JEV in the 0.2-0.8 gray zone. That would make the gate feel instant for 80% of calls.\nACCEPTANCE: obvious hit/miss cases return in <1s warm with the same verdicts; gray-zone cases may keep the JEV round-trip. Do not regress verdict quality (0.95 hit / 0.03 miss discrimination is the baseline to keep)."}
