 {"id": "AUG-065", "title": "[P2] SCOPE: auger — decide what connecting over the muster protocol means for this service", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 2, "status": "pending", "created_at": "2026-09-24T15:16:47Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T15:16:47Z", "reasoning": "CONTEXT — what \"connect over muster\" means here (read before scoping).\n\nmuster (github.com/wojons/muster) turns any OpenAPI 3.x spec into a typed CLI\n(openapi-cli), an MCP server (openapi-mcp), a daemon, and a Go library. A consumer\nattaches with one config block:\n\n  {\"mcpServers\": {\"<name>\": {\"command\": \"openapi-mcp\",\n                             \"args\": [\"--spec\", \"<url-or-path>\", \"--base-url\", \"<api>\"]}}}\n\n(muster README \"mcpServers\" + docs/integration-guide.md §2; verified 2026-09-24.)\n\nDESIGN AUTHORITY for every protocol row: muster/specs/PROTOCOLS.md — \"no protocol\nimplementation row may start before its adapter satisfies this spec's pipeline and\ncross-cutting contracts on paper\". The pipeline is discover/ingest -> protocol-neutral\noperation model -> SHARED command+MCP generation -> per-protocol transport executor.\nOpenAPI 3.x is the FIRST adapter, not the engine. muster's board carries PROTO-001..008.\n\n\"Support for people to connect to us over the muster protocol\" therefore means, for this\nproject: (1) publish a muster-consumable OpenAPI 3.x contract for our own service,\n(2) ship the consumer config + a human quickstart, (3) PROVE muster's own binaries\ningest it and drive the live service. Nothing here re-implements muster — we consume it.\n\n             THIS ROW IS ONE THIRD OF A CHAIN (scope -> spec -> build) filed together\n2026-09-24 at the operator's request. Do not start this row until its predecessor\nhas landed; the spec row must not invent a surface the scope row has not decided, and\nthe build row must not guess a contract the spec row has not frozen.\n\n             MEASURED STATE OF AUGER TODAY (2026-09-24, read from the live tree):\n\n             auger has NO HTTP server at all — measured 2026-09-24: no serve verb, no http.server/HTTPServer\nbind in auger.py. It is a stdlib-only Python CLI (`python3 auger.py -n <ns> <verb>`, 13 verbs)\nthat rides DuckBrain's declared-tables HTTP API on 127.0.0.1:3000 and calls JEV for judging.\nSo auger is the one target where \"connect over muster\" has no obvious referent, and the scope\ndecision is load-bearing. The three real options:\n  (a) EXPOSE auger: add a local HTTP API over the verbs (init/ask/answer/status/dump/recall/...)\n      and publish a spec for THAT. Most work, most value — agents could drill a spec over MCP.\n  (b) EXPOSE THE SUBSTRATE: publish the DuckBrain table API contract, which auger already rides.\n      Cheap, but it exposes the database, not auger's method — probably the wrong product.\n  (c) WRAP THE CLI: ship a muster-visible wrapper so an agent drives auger's verbs as tools\n      without any HTTP surface on auger at all. Least code; weakest typing.\nRelevant prior art in-repo: AUG-052 (split question generation from judgement) and the JEV\ndependency mean any exposed surface inherits two external dependencies (DuckBrain token, JEV key)\n— the scope must say how a muster consumer authenticates to those.\n\n             Specific scope questions: choose (a), (b) or (c) with the reason recorded. If (a): which verbs are\nread-only (status/dump/recall/check/ask) versus mutating (answer/toggle/propagate/feedback/verdict) —\nthe mutating half writes decisions into DuckBrain and must be MCP-gated. Also decide whether the\nspec is generated from the argparse registry (one source of truth, matching this repo's existing\ndiscipline) or hand-written, and how auth to the two external dependencies is carried by a muster\nclient that only knows how to send HTTP headers.\n\n             DELIVERABLE — a written scope, on this row (no code):\n             1. the surface we expose and why that surface (and, explicitly, what we do NOT expose)\n             2. the exact muster consumer block (the mcpServers entry with its real --spec path/URL\n                and --base-url) written out verbatim\n             3. the acceptance test for the later rows: the precise commands a verifier runs, and\n                the assertions that make them non-vacuous\n             4. the boundary call: which operations are agent-safe through MCP and which must be\n                gated (muster's MCP safety contract — mutating operations an agent should not\n                reach unattended)\n             5. the auth story: this service's credential/header vs what muster's config can carry\n\n             ACCEPTANCE: the row closes with the five items above present and concrete enough\n             that the spec row needs no new decision. If a real decision is still open, say so\n             and name who rules on it.", "capability_tags": ["+integration", "+protocol", "+interop"], "attempts": 0, "blocked_reason": null, "blocked_since": null, "blocks": [], "ci_result": null, "commit_hash": null, "completed_at": null, "depends_on": [], "dispatched_at": null, "exit_code": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "files_changed": [], "foreman_note": null, "guard_result": null, "perpetual": null, "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "review_notes": null, "worker_status": "pending", "worker_summary": null, "detail": {"fingerprint": "24bc1f57fa28f71390c8296d592d461f1e169ab7442de72f901bf2f13ab9fc76"}, "worktree": null, "branch": null, "superseded_by": null}
 {"id": "AUG-066", "title": "[P2] SPEC: auger — author the OpenAPI 3.x contract muster consumes, plus the consumer wiring", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 2, "status": "pending", "created_at": "2026-09-24T15:16:47Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T15:16:47Z", "reasoning": "CONTEXT — what \"connect over muster\" means here (read before scoping).\n\nmuster (github.com/wojons/muster) turns any OpenAPI 3.x spec into a typed CLI\n(openapi-cli), an MCP server (openapi-mcp), a daemon, and a Go library. A consumer\nattaches with one config block:\n\n  {\"mcpServers\": {\"<name>\": {\"command\": \"openapi-mcp\",\n                             \"args\": [\"--spec\", \"<url-or-path>\", \"--base-url\", \"<api>\"]}}}\n\n(muster README \"mcpServers\" + docs/integration-guide.md §2; verified 2026-09-24.)\n\nDESIGN AUTHORITY for every protocol row: muster/specs/PROTOCOLS.md — \"no protocol\nimplementation row may start before its adapter satisfies this spec's pipeline and\ncross-cutting contracts on paper\". The pipeline is discover/ingest -> protocol-neutral\noperation model -> SHARED command+MCP generation -> per-protocol transport executor.\nOpenAPI 3.x is the FIRST adapter, not the engine. muster's board carries PROTO-001..008.\n\n\"Support for people to connect to us over the muster protocol\" therefore means, for this\nproject: (1) publish a muster-consumable OpenAPI 3.x contract for our own service,\n(2) ship the consumer config + a human quickstart, (3) PROVE muster's own binaries\ningest it and drive the live service. Nothing here re-implements muster — we consume it.\n\n             THIS ROW IS ONE THIRD OF A CHAIN (scope -> spec -> build) filed together\n2026-09-24 at the operator's request. Do not start this row until its predecessor\nhas landed; the spec row must not invent a surface the scope row has not decided, and\nthe build row must not guess a contract the spec row has not frozen.\n\n             Spec work: whatever the scope chose, the contract must state where the auger CLI and the exposed\nsurface can drift and how that is checked — auger's argv surface is the product today, so a spec\nthat describes a surface nobody tests against the CLI is the drift risk to design out.\n\n             DELIVERABLE — the contract and the wiring, frozen on this row:\n             1. the OpenAPI 3.x document muster will be pointed at (file or served route), with its\n                location named precisely and its generation rule stated (hand-written vs generated\n                from the route table — this repo's own doctrine decides which)\n             2. operationIds, request/response schemas, and the servers[] url that muster dereferences\n                (muster falls back to the spec's own servers[].url when --base-url is omitted; a\n                RELATIVE servers url cannot be dereferenced standalone — say which case applies)\n             3. the consumer config block + a three-line human quickstart (the CLI form:\n                openapi-cli <generated-verb>), both added to this repo's docs\n             4. the parity rule: what keeps the spec from drifting off the real routes, in the\n                same shape as this repo's existing drift checks\n\n             ACCEPTANCE: the spec parses in muster's own parser, the consumer block is copy-pasteable,\n             and the parity rule is expressed as an executable check (not a comment).", "capability_tags": ["+integration", "+protocol", "+interop"], "attempts": 0, "blocked_reason": null, "blocked_since": null, "blocks": [], "ci_result": null, "commit_hash": null, "completed_at": null, "depends_on": ["AUG-065"], "dispatched_at": null, "exit_code": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "files_changed": [], "foreman_note": null, "guard_result": null, "perpetual": null, "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "review_notes": null, "worker_status": "pending", "worker_summary": null, "detail": {"fingerprint": "ab680d81435f3c2296e52e5459c5e8baa4a792af225db2f940cc95e016253fe0"}, "worktree": null, "branch": null, "superseded_by": null}
