t a health check — e.g. a\ngenerated tool that records a decision or returns a namespace's status map, with the DuckBrain\nnamespace named. If the scope chose (c), prove the wrapper drives the real CLI and that a refusal\n(unknown option, unknown namespace) surfaces as a tool error rather than a silent success.\n\n             DELIVERABLE — implementation plus a LIVE proof:\n             1. land the spec + parity check the spec row froze\n             2. build muster from source and demonstrate its OWN binaries against this service:\n                - `openapi-mcp --spec <ours>` → the typed tools are listed and at least one READ tool\n                  executes against the live service and returns real data\n                - `openapi-cli <generated-verb>` → a typed command executes and prints a real response\n                - the generated CLI must be driven through the documented invocation, not a bespoke\n                  shell script standing in for it\n             3. paste the raw output of both as this row's evidence, with the exact commands\n             4. name any operation muster generates that an agent should NOT be given, and how it is\n                withheld (per the scope row's boundary call)\n\n             ACCEPTANCE: a verifier who has never seen this repo can reproduce the two muster\n             binaries working against the live service from the row's own text. A spec that parses\n             but whose generated tools fail against the service is a FAIL, not a partial.\n\n             NOTE: muster is PRIVATE (github.com/wojons/muster) — the build row needs GOPRIVATE +\n             GitHub auth; record the working incantation in the row.", "capability_tags": ["+integration", "+protocol", "+interop"], "attempts": 0, "blocked_reason": null, "blocked_since": null, "blocks": [], "ci_result": null, "commit_hash": null, "completed_at": null, "depends_on": ["AUG-066"], "dispatched_at": null, "exit_code": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provi